{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-1340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $u=⟨-3,2⟩$ and $v=⟨7,9⟩.$ Find $u\\cdot v.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-1340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot 7+2\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =-21+18 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-1340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdbd9d771f26b0f33874b2ff84d12f4f643bfd2998f05aeeb31d3b4632f8feea"} {"question" "q-1340" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-1340" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "39"] ["math" "57"] ["math" "63"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-1340" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $a=⟨5,1⟩$ and $b=⟨2,4⟩,$ then $a\\cdot b=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =10+4 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdbd9d771f26b0f33874b2ff84d12f4f643bfd2998f05aeeb31d3b4632f8feea"} {"question" "q-317910" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317910" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-1341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $\\overset{\\to }{a}=⟨1,-2,4⟩$ and $\\overset{\\to }{b}=⟨11,4,-1⟩$, then $\\overset{\\to }{a}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{b}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-1341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{a}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{b} & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 11+(-2)\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =11+(-8)+(-4) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-1341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdbd9d771f26b0f33874b2ff84d12f4f643bfd2998f05aeeb31d3b4632f8feea"} {"question" "q-1341" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-1341" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "27"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-1341" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-101406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨1,-2⟩$ and $q=⟨4,-1⟩.$ Find $p\\cdot q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-101406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4+(-2)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =4+2 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-101406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdbd9d771f26b0f33874b2ff84d12f4f643bfd2998f05aeeb31d3b4632f8feea"} {"question" "q-101406" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-101406" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-101406" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317911" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $u=⟨8,-2⟩$ and $v=⟨3,6⟩,$ then $u\\cdot v=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317911" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y} \\\\  & =8\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24-12 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317911" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdbd9d771f26b0f33874b2ff84d12f4f643bfd2998f05aeeb31d3b4632f8feea"} {"question" "q-317911" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317911" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $c=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 2k \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ $d=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ and $c⊥d,$ then $k=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $c⊥d$ ($c$ and $d$ are perpendicular) if and only if $c\\cdot d=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot d & ={c}_{x}\\cdot {d}_{x}+{c}_{y}\\cdot {d}_{y}+{c}_{z}\\cdot {d}_{z} \\\\  & =k\\cdot (-3)+2k\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-3k+4k+8 \\\\  & =k+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot d & =0 \\\\ k+8 & =0 \\\\ k & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdbd9d771f26b0f33874b2ff84d12f4f643bfd2998f05aeeb31d3b4632f8feea"} {"question" "q-317932" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317932" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-1348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ n\\end{aligned}]$ and $q=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $p⊥q$, find the value of $n.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-1348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $p⊥q$ ($p$ and $q$ are perpendicular) if and only if $p\\cdot q=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y} \\\\  & =7\\cdot 4+n\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =28-4n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 28-4n & =0 \\\\ 28 & =4n \\\\ n & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-1348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdbd9d771f26b0f33874b2ff84d12f4f643bfd2998f05aeeb31d3b4632f8feea"} {"question" "q-1348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-1348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-7"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-1348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2{x}^{2},-4⟩$ and $b=⟨8,4⟩.$ If $a⊥b$ and $x>0,$ then $x=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $a⊥b$ ($a$ and $b$ are perpendicular) if and only if $a\\cdot b=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}\\cdot 8+(-4)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =16{x}^{2}-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ 16{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are told that $x>0.$ Therefore, $x=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdbd9d771f26b0f33874b2ff84d12f4f643bfd2998f05aeeb31d3b4632f8feea"} {"question" "q-317945" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-317945" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-19023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $g=[\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2} \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$ and $h=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ {r}^{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r<0$, find the value of $r.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-19023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & ={r}^{2}\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot {r}^{2}+(-6)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3{r}^{2}-{r}^{2}-12 \\\\  & =2{r}^{2}-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 2{r}^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} & =12 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =6 \\\\ r & =\\pm \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $r<0.$ Therefore, $r=-\\sqrt{6}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-19023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdbd9d771f26b0f33874b2ff84d12f4f643bfd2998f05aeeb31d3b4632f8feea"} {"question" "q-19023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-19023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "-\\sqrt{12}"] ["math" "-\\sqrt{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-19023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\sqrt{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-77152" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $u⊥v$ and $a<0$, find the value of $a.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-77152" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $u⊥v$ ($u$ and $v$ are perpendicular) if and only if $u\\cdot v=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y}+{u}_{z}\\cdot {v}_{z} \\\\  & =a\\cdot a+2\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & ={a}^{2}-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =16 \\\\ a & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $a<0.$ Therefore, $a=-4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-77152" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdbd9d771f26b0f33874b2ff84d12f4f643bfd2998f05aeeb31d3b4632f8feea"} {"question" "q-77152" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-77152" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "-9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "q-77152" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/state.json" "file_sha256" "59e5324f1deefc93303980c08ae208684c528f4619822becbac45e7c2201cb21"} {"question" "e-4323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 0,-0.4,11 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 2,5,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/example-4323.json" "file_sha256" "d3d970e290a8643a97e84ace142fce2530f67724dc2e729931ec39d4a7dfc242"} {"question" "e-4323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 2+(-0.4)\\cdot 5+11\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =0-2+22 \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/example-4323.json" "file_sha256" "d3d970e290a8643a97e84ace142fce2530f67724dc2e729931ec39d4a7dfc242"} {"question" "e-4324" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ t\\end{aligned}]$. Given that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$, find the value of $t$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/example-4324.json" "file_sha256" "934ea555648572086cba1adbf910fa2b14d57c89969a5c52306e2e2a0ddffa08"} {"question" "e-4324" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$ ($\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are perpendicular) if and only if $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot t \\\\  & =-8-10+t \\\\  & =t-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ t-18 & =0 \\\\ t & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035976/example-4324.json" "file_sha256" "934ea555648572086cba1adbf910fa2b14d57c89969a5c52306e2e2a0ddffa08"}] "usage" {"e-4323" [] "q-1340" [] "e-4324" []} "basis" 1245 "retractions" [[17592186059952 :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{u} = \\langle  - 3 , 2 \\rangle$ and $v = \\langle 7, 9\\rangle $. Find $u \\cdot v$."] [17592186059467 :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 0,-0.4,11 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 2,5,2 \\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}$."] [17592186059467 :question/worked-solution "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  \\mathbf{b} & = {a}_{x} \\cdot  {b}_{x} + {a}_{y} \\cdot  {b}_{y} + {a}_{z} \\cdot  {b}_{z} \\\\  & = 0 \\cdot  2 + ( - 0.4 ) \\cdot  5 + 11 \\cdot  2 \\\\  & = 0 - 2 + 22 \\\\  & = 20\\end{array}$$"] [17592186059468 :question/problem "Let \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a} = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c}4 \\\\ - 2 \\\\ 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n and \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b} = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ t\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n. Given that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$, find the value of $t$."] [17592186059468 :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$ ($\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are perpendicular) if and only if\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 0\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  \\mathbf{b} & = {a}_{x} \\cdot  {b}_{x} + {a}_{y} \\cdot  {b}_{y} + {a}_{z} \\cdot  {b}_{z} \\\\  & = 4 \\cdot  ( - 2 ) + ( - 2 ) \\cdot  5 + 1 \\cdot  t \\\\  & = - 8 - 10 + t \\\\  & = t - 18.\\end{array}$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0$, we obtain:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  \\mathbf{b} & = 0 \\\\ t - 18 & = 0 \\\\ t & = 18\\end{array}$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186056432 17592186056433 17592186056434 17592186056435 17592186056436] "immutable_fields" [[17592186056431 :answer-field/correct] [17592186056431 :answer-field/id] [17592186056431 :answer-field/key] [17592186056431 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
